00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:34,759
Okay, I'm just going to
write this out to cash.

268
00:10:34,759 --> 00:10:36,719
Okay?

269
00:10:36,719 --> 00:10:38,012
Hi, Mona.
Hey.

270
00:10:38,012 --> 00:10:41,433
Hi.
Oh, hey.

271
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:43,101
Joey's going to be thrilled.

272
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:45,061
He was hoping you'd come by
as a slutty nurse.

273
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:48,773
Um, actually,
I'm just a nurse.

274
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:51,818
You'd think that
would embarrass me

275
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:54,237
but you see, I'm maxed out.

276
00:10:55,989 --> 00:10:58,158
MONA:
Hi.
Hey, you made it.

277
00:10:58,158 --> 00:11:00,034
Wait, wait. You're, um...
you're a potato.

278
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:02,703
Well, I'm a spud...

279
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:04,623
And the antennae...

280
00:11:04,623 --> 00:11:06,207
Oh, my God, you're Sputnik!

281
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:07,292
Yes!

282
00:11:07,292 --> 00:11:08,876
Marry her.

283
00:11:10,753 --> 00:11:12,547
Okay, here's
a good one for you.

284
00:11:12,547 --> 00:11:14,424
Who do you think
would win in a fight

285
00:11:14,424 --> 00:11:16,134
between Ross and Chandler?

286
00:11:16,134 --> 00:11:18,470
I can't answer that--
Chandler is my husband.

287
00:11:18,470 --> 00:11:19,596
So, Ross?

288
00:11:19,596 --> 00:11:21,431
Yeah.

289
00:11:21,431 --> 00:11:23,141
Hey, beautiful.

290
00:11:23,141 --> 00:11:24,976
Hello, handsome.

291
00:11:24,976 --> 00:11:26,394
Oh, God.

292
00:11:27,646 --> 00:11:29,230
Oh, look at you two.

293
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:31,399
So, when did
you guys meet?

294
00:11:31,399 --> 00:11:32,526
Two weeks ago.

295
00:11:32,526 --> 00:11:33,943
Two weeks, that's it?

296
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:35,654
Yeah, I know it sounds crazy

297
00:11:35,654 --> 00:11:37,405
and it's not like me
to do something so impulsive

298
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:41,159
but she's just so perfect,
and we have so much in common.

299
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:42,410
Oh, really?

300
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:43,953
We're both teachers.

301
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:44,912
Huh?

302
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:48,333
And we were both
in the Peace Corps.

303
00:11:48,333 --> 00:11:49,834
Peace Corps, really?

304
00:11:52,504 --> 00:11:55,382
In fact, when we were
building houses in Uruguay

305
00:11:55,382 --> 00:11:59,093
we were just two towns apart
and we never met.

306
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:01,262
Yeah. It wasn't a town
when I got there

307
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:02,972
but it was a town
when I left.

308
00:12:05,016 --> 00:12:06,809
Shall we get me
really drunk?

309
00:12:06,809 --> 00:12:08,395
Sure.

310
00:12:08,395 --> 00:12:11,565
( forced chuckle )

311
00:12:13,692 --> 00:12:16,570
Howdy, Doody.

312
00:12:16,570 --> 00:12:18,071
That's funny, yeah.

313
00:12:18,071 --> 00:12:20,365
You know, you're
the funniest man here

314
00:12:20,365 --> 00:12:23,410
in a pink bunny costume
his wife made him wear.

315
00:12:23,410 --> 00:12:25,119
Relax, man, relax.

316
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:27,997
You're looking
a little flushed.

317
00:12:32,335 --> 00:12:33,794
I think we
might find out

318
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:35,422
the answer
to our question.

319
00:12:35,422 --> 00:12:36,673
What question?

320
00:12:36,673 --> 00:12:38,258
Monica and I were
talking about

321
00:12:38,258 --> 00:12:40,427
who could kick whose ass
in a fight, you or Ross.

322
00:12:40,427 --> 00:12:42,303
There's no question.

323
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:44,514
So you think Ross, too?

324
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:48,351
You picked Ross?!

325
00:12:48,351 --> 00:12:49,768
Ross is really strong.

326
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:52,188
He's the strongest out
of all three of you

327
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:54,815
except for Joey.

328
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:57,318
I cannot believe
you didn't pick me.

329
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:59,279
In her defense,
she's right.

330
00:12:59,279 --> 00:13:01,740
I am stronger;
I would destroy you.

331
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:04,242
Oh, really? You think
you're stronger?

332
00:13:04,242 --> 00:13:05,784
Why don't you prove it?

333
00:13:08,246 --> 00:13:09,372
Oh, I'll prove it!

334
00:13:09,372 --> 00:13:11,165
I'll prove it
like a theorem!

335
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:12,542
MONICA:
Wait, wait, wait!

336
00:13:12,542 --> 00:13:13,543
Okay, stop it!

337
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:15,211
Stop it! Stop!

338
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:16,879
Now, no one's going to fight
in this apartment!

339
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:18,923
Hey, Monica, people
came to see a fight.

340
00:13:18,923 --> 00:13:20,717
Let's give them
what they came for.

341
00:13:20,717 --> 00:13:21,884
Yeah!

342
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:23,844
You guys could arm wrestle.

343
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:27,181
Yeah, listen
to the slutty nurse.

344
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:29,309
You're going down.

345
00:13:29,309 --> 00:13:32,312
You're going further down--
downtown!

346
00:13:32,312 --> 00:13:35,356
Seriously, guys,
the trash talk is embarrassing.

347
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:45,617
Oh, Gunther,
you brought candy.

348
00:13:45,617 --> 00:13:47,494
Thank you so much
for picking this up.

349
00:13:47,494 --> 00:13:48,620
You are so sweet.

350
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,246
Really?
Yeah.

351
00:13:50,246 --> 00:13:52,582
Someday you are going
to make some man

352
00:13:52,582 --> 00:13:54,501
the luckiest guy in the world.

353
00:13:54,501 --> 00:13:55,794
( knock at door )
Got to go.

354
00:13:55,794 --> 00:13:57,754
BOY:
Trick or treat.

355
00:13:58,879 --> 00:13:59,922
Hi!

356
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:01,132
Wow.

357
00:14:01,132 --> 00:14:02,801
There you go.

358
00:14:02,801 --> 00:14:06,053
My friend Louis told me
you were giving out money.

359
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:10,600
Oh, yeah, well, we were,
but now we've got candy.

360
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:13,894
I'd rather have the money.

361
00:14:13,894 --> 00:14:16,606
Well, that-that's
not your choice.

362
00:14:16,606 --> 00:14:17,856
Happy Halloween.

363
00:14:17,856 --> 00:14:19,526
This isn't fair.

364
00:14:19,526 --> 00:14:21,611
Well, is it fair that all
you did was put on a cape

365
00:14:21,611 --> 00:14:22,987
and I got to give
you free stuff?

366
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:23,988
Shut up.

367
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:26,949
You shut up.

368
00:14:28,576 --> 00:14:30,537
You can't tell me to shut up.

369
00:14:30,537 --> 00:14:32,455
Uh... I think I just did

370
00:14:32,455 --> 00:14:35,750
and, uh-oh, here it
comes again: Shut up.

371
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:37,168
Uh, Rache.

372
00:14:37,168 --> 00:14:38,795
Yeah. I got it.
I'm good. I got it.

373
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:43,174
Now, wait a minute,
I had one more thing

374
00:14:43,174 --> 00:14:45,885
I had to say to you:
Oh, right. Shut up.

375
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:47,970
You're a mean old woman.

376
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:50,014
Oh, wait. No. Shut up--
I mean, don't cry.

377
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:52,350
Let me get my checkbook.

378
00:14:52,350 --> 00:14:54,728
Look, honey, you don't
have to do this, okay?

379
00:14:54,728 --> 00:14:56,604
It's the strength
you have inside

380
00:14:56,604 --> 00:14:58,147
that means
the most to me.

381
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:00,400
I mean, you're loyal
and you're honest

382
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,193
and you have integrity.

383
00:15:02,193 --> 00:15:04,487
That's the kind of strength
I want in the man I love.

384
00:15:04,487 --> 00:15:06,531
That means nothing to me.

385
00:15:06,531 --> 00:15:08,616
Come on!

386
00:15:08,616 --> 00:15:10,410
Aah.

387
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:11,536
Hi, liar.

388
00:15:11,536 --> 00:15:12,537
Hey.

389
00:15:12,537 --> 00:15:13,747
You know...

390
00:15:13,747 --> 00:15:15,331
the only reason
he's marrying you

391
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:17,083
is because he thinks
all the things

392
00:15:17,083 --> 00:15:19,210
you were saying
about yourself were true.

393
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:20,420
Well, they could be true.

394
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:22,004
But they're not.

395
00:15:22,004 --> 00:15:24,549
Yeah. It's a
fine line, huh?

396
00:15:24,549 --> 00:15:26,593
Why are you lying to him?

397
00:15:26,593 --> 00:15:27,926
I don't know.

398
00:15:27,926 --> 00:15:29,512
He said he did
all this stuff

399
00:15:29,512 --> 00:15:31,097
and then I said
I did it, too

400
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:33,307
and he got so excited,
it was really fun.

401
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:34,559
Honey?

402
00:15:34,559 --> 00:15:36,977
It's a filthy,
disgusting habit

403
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:39,647
and I want you
to quit now.

404
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:42,442
She's helped so many
people quit smoking.

405
00:15:42,442 --> 00:15:44,985
You know, we really
better get going.

406
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:46,654
You have a church
group meeting tonight.

407
00:15:46,654 --> 00:15:48,114
Right.

408
00:15:50,825 --> 00:15:53,494
Well, it was nice
meeting you.

409
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:54,537
You, too.

410
00:15:56,163 --> 00:16:00,293
And, Ursula, it was really nice
meeting you tonight!

411
00:16:00,293 --> 00:16:01,294
Phebes, come on.

412
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:02,378
Bunny versus Doody.

413
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:03,337
We're waiting.

414
00:16:06,006 --> 00:16:07,508
Okay. Okay, guys.

415
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:09,886
One match, winner take all.

416
00:16:09,886 --> 00:16:11,178
Wait, wait.

417
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:12,889
What does the winner get?

418
00:16:12,889 --> 00:16:14,557
Pride.

419
00:16:14,557 --> 00:16:15,642
And dignity.

420
00:16:15,642 --> 00:16:18,227
Okay, if you say so.

421
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:19,562
All right, ready?

422
00:16:19,562 --> 00:16:20,730
Set, go.

423
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:24,066
( crowd cheering )

424
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:25,359
Doody! Bunny!

425
00:16:29,948 --> 00:16:33,159
Wow, they're both
really strong.

426
00:16:33,159 --> 00:16:36,162
Or equally weak.

427
00:16:36,162 --> 00:16:37,580
Oh, my God.

428
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:40,082
Chandler's making
his sex face.

429
00:16:44,671 --> 00:16:47,173
So, are you getting tired?

430
00:16:47,173 --> 00:16:51,093
Nope. I can do this all day.

431
00:16:51,093 --> 00:16:55,014
Yeah, me, too.

432
00:16:55,014 --> 00:16:57,016
I'm getting a
little tired, though.

433
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:58,935
God, I'm exhausted.

434
00:16:58,935 --> 00:17:02,605
Look, this is starting
to look really bad for me.

435
00:17:02,605 --> 00:17:06,108
Okay, Mona... Mona's standing
right over there.

436
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:08,778
Oh, God, she's
talking to Joey.

437
00:17:08,778 --> 00:17:10,446
You got to let me win.

438
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:12,239
Wait, if anything,
you've to let me win.

439
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:13,449
My wife thinks I'm a wimp.

440
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:15,284
Hey, at least you have a wife.

441
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:18,120
I keep getting divorces
and knocking people up.

442
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:23,751
And I'm dressed as Doody.

443
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:26,379
You're Spudnik.

444
00:17:26,379 --> 00:17:28,339
Come on,
who are we kidding?

445
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:29,924
I'm Doody.

446
00:17:29,924 --> 00:17:31,968
Please, she's watching.

447
00:17:31,968 --> 00:17:33,427
( sighs )

448
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:35,221
Fine.

449
00:17:36,848 --> 00:17:38,016
( grunts loudly )

450
00:17:38,016 --> 00:17:39,017
Oh, no.
Oh, no.

451
00:17:39,017 --> 00:17:40,226
Oh, yeah!

452
00:17:40,226 --> 00:17:42,144
Yay!

453
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:44,104
My hero.

454
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:45,565
You're a weird lady.

455
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:51,821
Hey, Ursula said
she left her purse.

456
00:17:51,821 --> 00:17:52,822
Oh.

457
00:17:52,822 --> 00:17:54,448
Oh, what a relief.

458
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:56,743
It has all the numbers of
the people in the prayer chain.

459
00:17:56,743 --> 00:17:59,078
Sure it does. Yeah, yeah.

460
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:01,039
Well, I guess
I'll see you at the wedding.

461
00:18:03,081 --> 00:18:05,001
Um, listen, I
don't think...

462
00:18:05,001 --> 00:18:07,378
I don't think I'm going to
make it to the wedding, so...

463
00:18:07,378 --> 00:18:09,756
I just want to wish you
all the luck in the world.

464
00:18:09,756 --> 00:18:11,090
I think we'll be okay.

465
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:12,967
Besides, it's so perfect and...

466
00:18:12,967 --> 00:18:15,803
( whispering ):
she's been saving
herself for me.

467
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:19,181
Okay, I can't
let you do this.

468
00:18:19,181 --> 00:18:20,349
She's lying to you.

469
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:21,893
What?

470
00:18:21,893 --> 00:18:23,978
She is lying, and I
bet I can prove it.

471
00:18:23,978 --> 00:18:25,772
Excuse me.

472
00:18:25,772 --> 00:18:27,857
Okay. Okay.

473
00:18:27,857 --> 00:18:29,525
Yeah. Not a
prayer chain

474
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:32,152
but what looks like
a detailed drawing

475
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:33,613
of a bank floor plan.

476
00:18:35,197 --> 00:18:36,866
Okay, here's
the name tag

477
00:18:36,866 --> 00:18:38,242
from the restaurant

478
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:40,369
where she works
as a waitress.

479
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:42,872
Not a teacher,
a waitress.

480
00:18:42,872 --> 00:18:44,540
All right, here's
her driver's license.

481
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:45,708
This ought to be good.

482
00:18:45,708 --> 00:18:46,876
She always lies
about this.

483
00:18:46,876 --> 00:18:47,877
How old did she
say she was?

484
00:18:47,877 --> 00:18:49,462
She told me she was 25.

485
00:18:49,462 --> 00:18:52,048
Oh. I almost don't
want to show you this.

486
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:56,719
Just remember, I'm
a minute younger.

487
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:01,015
I am so stupid.

488
00:19:01,015 --> 00:19:03,059
Of course she was lying.

489
00:19:03,059 --> 00:19:04,852
She's not a teacher.

490
00:19:04,852 --> 00:19:07,480
There's no such thing as
the top secret elementary school

491
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,816
for the children of spies.

492
00:19:11,734 --> 00:19:14,278
No, you're not,
you're not stupid.

493
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:16,196
I'm not smart.

494
00:19:20,326 --> 00:19:25,289
I just wanted so much
to be impulsive for once.

495
00:19:25,289 --> 00:19:26,916
To be romantic.

496
00:19:26,916 --> 00:19:28,001
That's good.

497
00:19:28,001 --> 00:19:29,127
You should
be impulsive

498
00:19:29,127 --> 00:19:30,544
and you should
be romantic.

499
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:33,547
Just... you did it
with the wrong person.

500
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:37,051
What?

501
00:19:37,051 --> 00:19:41,848
It's so weird, two people look
so much alike... so different.

502
00:19:44,017 --> 00:19:45,643
Eric, let's go!

503
00:19:47,436 --> 00:19:49,229
I better go deal.

504
00:19:49,229 --> 00:19:50,690
Yeah, you should.

505
00:19:57,113 --> 00:19:59,532
Hurry up!
I got to pray!

506
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:11,085
Hey.
Hey.

507
00:20:11,085 --> 00:20:14,755
Well, I had to give the kid
50 bucks to stop crying.

508
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:16,924
Well, that's not so bad.

509
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:19,135
I also had to go
to a couple houses with him

510
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:20,094
as his girlfriend.

511
00:20:21,679 --> 00:20:24,473
Oh, I'm just awful
with children.

512
00:20:24,473 --> 00:20:26,475
Come on. You're
good with kids.

513
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:28,602
They're just crazy
on Halloween.

514
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:30,437
You know,
they're all greedy

515
00:20:30,437 --> 00:20:31,981
and hopped up on sugar.

516
00:20:31,981 --> 00:20:34,150
Really? You think
that's all it is?

517
00:20:34,150 --> 00:20:37,987
Absolutely. Halloween
is the worst.

518
00:20:37,987 --> 00:20:39,530
Except for Christmas.

519
00:20:39,530 --> 00:20:41,032
And their birthdays.

520
00:20:41,032 --> 00:20:42,241
Mm-hmm.

521
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:43,659
They kind of get
a little crazy

522
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:45,161
during the summer, too.

523
00:20:45,161 --> 00:20:48,206
And any time they're
hungry or sleepy.

524
00:20:48,206 --> 00:20:50,124
Yeah, kids are tough.

525
00:20:50,124 --> 00:20:51,918
Good luck with that.

526
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:59,383
Look, I wanted to tell you,
I'm, I'm sorry you lost.

527
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:03,303
Oh. Listen, I got a secret
for you: I let him win.

528
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:05,681
Is that a secret
or a lie?

529
00:21:05,681 --> 00:21:08,726
No, I let him... Ross.

530
00:21:08,726 --> 00:21:11,187
Would you tell her
that I let you win, please?

531
00:21:11,187 --> 00:21:12,312
Oh, yeah.

532
00:21:12,312 --> 00:21:14,899
Uh, Chandler "let" me win.

533
00:21:16,734 --> 00:21:18,569
No, Chandler's really strong.

534
00:21:18,569 --> 00:21:19,946
Oh, my arm is so sore.

535
00:21:19,946 --> 00:21:20,988
Oh, nurse!

536
00:21:22,615 --> 00:21:23,824
I am strong.

537
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:25,243
I'll show you.

538
00:21:26,284 --> 00:21:27,745
Chandler, please.

539
00:21:27,745 --> 00:21:28,829
Oh, what's the matter?

540
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:29,872
Are you scared?

541
00:21:29,872 --> 00:21:32,416
Let's go, Big Bunny!

542
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:36,170
One, two, three. Go.

543
00:21:41,383 --> 00:21:43,886
I'm going to kill myself.

